at all. So I thought that was really nice to like actually get a chance to like learn the ropes

00:12:55.100 --> 00:12:58.540
and figure out like, what's the difference between locking on enemies versus just shooting

00:12:58.540 --> 00:13:01.500
on them? Like, how can I, how can I best take down people?

00:13:02.100 --> 00:13:05.360
And I was just having so much fun that I hoped I never had to land my plane.

00:13:05.580 --> 00:13:12.720
And you are. Well, before we get into like the gameplay itself, I did have a quick tale from the manual.

00:13:12.900 --> 00:13:15.040
I would love to go into a little tales from the manual.

00:13:15.260 --> 00:13:21.260
What do you got? So, a lot of video games start with a little bit of a, of a deep lore.

00:13:21.600 --> 00:13:29.440
And this one starts with what, it starts out as like a second person omniscient story

00:13:29.440 --> 00:13:35.420
of you, the pilot, getting ready to get on, to get in your plane and do some really cool

00:13:35.420 --> 00:13:40.600
dog fighting. And then somewhere in the middle, it changes to a letter from the president.

00:13:41.060 --> 00:13:45.920
Like it starts with snug in the cockpit of a $30 million war machine.

00:13:46.140 --> 00:13:51.060
You ease the control stick forward and aim the plane's nose toward the center of the runway.

00:13:51.360 --> 00:13:52.960
And then yada, yada, yada, yada.

00:13:53.280 --> 00:13:56.320
And then remember the entire free world will be flying with you.

00:13:56.420 --> 00:13:58.460
If you succeed, World War three will be averted.

00:13:58.480 --> 00:14:00.440
If you fail, may God help us all.

00:14:00.580 --> 00:14:02.200
Good luck. Signed, Mr.

00:14:02.400 --> 00:14:06.160
President. He was just trying to set the mood for you in the beginning of the letter.

00:14:06.220 --> 00:14:07.060
And then you gotta read the line.

00:14:07.080 --> 00:14:08.980
You didn't even notice that. You gotta read the line after that though.

00:14:09.400 --> 00:14:11.460
And then P.S. You crumple the orders and eat them.

00:14:11.720 --> 00:14:14.840
No way. The president is just like lost it.

00:14:14.980 --> 00:14:17.280
It's like the Adam West president from Family Guy.

00:14:17.860 --> 00:14:19.240
Or the mayor or whatever it was.

00:14:19.600 --> 00:14:21.160
So I think that really sets the mood.

00:14:21.320 --> 00:14:23.140
I don't know if it's the correct mood for the movie.

00:14:23.660 --> 00:14:26.120
And you play as Maverick in the game, right?

00:14:26.120 --> 00:14:29.300
I guess. Yeah, I'm just saying like, is that in line with his character?

00:14:29.740 --> 00:14:32.280
What do you eat? Does he eat paper in the movie?

00:14:32.480 --> 00:14:35.560
I don't recall a scene where he like crumbled off a paper.

00:14:35.560 --> 00:14:39.020
He eats a letter from the president. I don't recall a letter from the president in the movie.

00:14:39.240 --> 00:14:43.360
So. I think this is just Konami plussing things up for video games.

00:14:43.460 --> 00:14:46.580
You know, like that's the kind of stuff where if I'm a kid and I'm reading that,

00:14:46.660 --> 00:14:48.480
I'm like, heck yeah. I eat paper.

00:14:48.820 --> 00:14:51.620
Like. Well, can I add to that too?

00:14:51.720 --> 00:14:56.900
Because when I read this, after this like intense intro, there's a big title that says

00:14:56.900 --> 00:14:58.900
How to Play. And I was like, this is going to get down to business.

00:14:59.060 --> 00:15:01.000
But then it still goes, strap in, lieutenant.

00:15:01.200 --> 00:15:04.120
Like it still goes back into the story.

00:15:04.320 --> 00:15:09.380
And then in the middle of it, it says, you begin the mission with three aircraft.

00:15:09.680 --> 00:15:14.660
The game, if you can call war a game, ends when you, it's just like telling you the

00:15:14.660 --> 00:15:19.080
instruction, but like still just committing to this like, this act.

00:15:19.280 --> 00:15:21.960
I love it. I think it's all very fun. I think it's a little too much information, right?

00:15:22.080 --> 00:15:24.320
Usually we just get like a little blurb or something.

00:15:24.520 --> 00:15:30.660
Yeah. This is just like, you know, paragraphs of exposition.

00:15:31.500 --> 00:15:34.040
Yeah. You know, to set up a game that does a pretty good job.

00:15:34.200 --> 00:15:39.840
I didn't have problems following along that I was like on missions to assignments to take

00:15:39.840 --> 00:15:41.720
down. Yeah, it tells you in the game what your mission is.

00:15:41.800 --> 00:15:44.980
Yeah, exactly. So I don't think I needed all this extra setup, but I'll take it.

00:15:45.120 --> 00:15:46.020
It's nice. It's in the manual.

00:15:46.720 --> 00:15:50.620
It's literature. If you're in the car on the way home, you're reading the manual and getting the story.

00:15:50.760 --> 00:15:53.780
Absolutely. That's a thing that is a shame that it's no longer around.

00:15:54.020 --> 00:15:56.400
I know. But also it wasn't exclusive to even this time period.

00:15:56.560 --> 00:15:58.680
I was doing that all the way up until like...

00:15:58.680 --> 00:15:59.760
2005. Yeah. PS2.

00:15:59.980 --> 00:16:01.940
I would do that even when I would have my own car.

00:16:02.540 --> 00:16:03.900
Yeah. I was driving over the side.

00:16:05.520 --> 00:16:07.180
Very unsafe. Let me read the manual.

00:16:08.240 --> 00:16:09.160
At the stoplight?

00:16:09.380 --> 00:16:12.220
Sure. They can arrest you for a crime you committed years ago.

00:16:13.240 --> 00:16:32.020
Ha! Ok! Ok!!

00:17:10.580 --> 00:17:11.980
All right.

00:17:11.980 --> 00:17:15.220
So we're going to jump into gameplay, but first I'm just going to set up the objective again.

00:17:15.220 --> 00:17:19.200
If you guys notice, I have a new format for the objective section based on last week's episode.

00:17:19.400 --> 00:17:21.860
Good job, Mike. Seems like people like that, so here I'm going to do it again.

00:17:22.340 --> 00:17:30.600
In Top Gun, you are maverick and must control your plane in a pseudo-3D environment to dogfight other planes through four missions.

00:17:31.040 --> 00:17:35.160
Once your mission is complete, you must land the plane onto an air carrier.

00:17:35.680 --> 00:17:38.980
Similar games include Star Voyager, as Joe mentioned earlier.

00:17:40.440 --> 00:17:47.580
I would like to say that the similarity to Star Voyager is pretty, like, that's on the surface.

00:17:48.060 --> 00:17:57.060
I would like to say that similar to how, I'm surprised you called this one out, but you didn't call out the Metroid thing too much in last week's episode when I said that Super Pitfall is like Metroid.

00:17:57.320 --> 00:18:00.600
I think it's just more like genre and vibe and stuff like that.

00:18:00.600 --> 00:18:05.780
I don't think it's like the game is, like, the same thing as Star Voyager.

00:18:06.040 --> 00:18:07.480
I'm just trying to give, like, a reference point.

00:18:07.480 --> 00:18:11.580
I understand. It's really kind of like the way it controls, the way it, like, literally looks.

00:18:11.800 --> 00:18:13.760
Yeah. And also, like, partially the way it controls.

00:18:13.860 --> 00:18:20.520
It's not a simulator. We really only had, like, two first-person-ish games, and I think those are the only two, so I will grant you that.

00:18:20.660 --> 00:18:24.320
Yes. I wasn't trying to say that you're looking for other planets in Top Gun.

00:18:24.340 --> 00:18:25.140
No, I understand.

00:18:25.140 --> 00:18:30.380
There is, like, automated takeoff and landing, though, in both of them.

00:18:30.460 --> 00:18:32.100
Yes, that's true. Well, automated?

00:18:32.560 --> 00:18:33.500
Well, to an extent.

00:18:33.680 --> 00:18:36.160
Like, there's a cutscene that plays when you're in landing mode.

00:18:36.300 --> 00:18:37.500
That's true. Okay, sure.

00:18:38.240 --> 00:18:40.960
So, before we talk about landing, look, that's going to be a whole discussion.

00:18:40.960 --> 00:18:41.960
I know it. I feel it already.

00:18:42.060 --> 00:18:44.440
Anybody who's listening to this episode who's played this game knows it's coming.

00:18:44.600 --> 00:18:45.940
They can feel it on the edge.

00:18:46.040 --> 00:18:48.720
They're probably skipping to that chapter marker right now.

00:18:48.960 --> 00:18:52.320
But instead, we're just going to talk about the dogfighting right now, okay?

00:18:53.260 --> 00:18:54.200
What did we think?

00:18:54.200 --> 00:19:00.100
We said in our first impressions that that was a pretty, like, convincing way to handle it on the NES.

00:19:00.300 --> 00:19:01.440
But was it actually fun?

00:19:01.940 --> 00:19:03.080
Yes, it was fun.

00:19:03.140 --> 00:19:06.520
And I think it's fun because they didn't try to be a simulation.

00:19:06.520 --> 00:19:13.360
This is very much an arcade game that sort of has bells and whistles that might make it look like a simulation.

00:19:15.220 --> 00:19:29.360
Because it's sort of like in that same realm of Tales of 3D World Runner where you have this illusion of control, like turning and stuff like that.

00:19:29.460 --> 00:19:31.260
But really, you're just always going forward.

00:19:31.260 --> 00:19:38.940
And if it were trying to be a simulation, you'd probably get stuck on trying to just center yourself.

00:19:39.320 --> 00:19:44.280
And I think that the simplification of a flight simulator works really well in this game.

00:19:44.880 --> 00:19:49.920
And I don't know if it was just me, but, like, I started at a certain altitude.

00:19:50.100 --> 00:19:54.320
And by the end of the dogfight, I was like 30,000, 40,000.

00:19:54.500 --> 00:19:57.960
I just continuously moved my aircraft higher and higher.

00:19:58.180 --> 00:19:59.760
Like, I never went down.

00:19:59.940 --> 00:20:05.080
I went down sometimes. I feel like it's better off being relatively low.

00:20:05.220 --> 00:20:06.340
I think that's part of the game.

00:20:06.480 --> 00:20:14.580
Part of it is feeling out if it's better to take on the battleships that are in the water or the planes that are in the air.

00:20:15.020 --> 00:20:22.460
Yeah. I actually didn't notice too much of a difference between at least the look of the game, depending on your altitude.

00:20:22.460 --> 00:20:26.900
I know that when you're doing air-to-ground combat, because there's three modes.

00:20:27.100 --> 00:20:30.880
There's dogfighting, air-to-ground, and air-to-sea.

00:20:31.800 --> 00:20:37.840
I guess the sprites might be bigger when it's on the ground or in the sea if you're lower.

00:20:38.040 --> 00:20:39.840
But I didn't really notice anything else.

00:20:40.060 --> 00:20:40.900
I didn't really either.

00:20:40.900 --> 00:20:42.460
I rarely looked at, like, my altitude.

00:20:42.600 --> 00:20:51.820
Yeah. And what do we think about, you know, fighting other ships, other spacecraft, fuck, like, all over the place today, guys?

00:20:51.820 --> 00:20:58.820
Like, other planes, how did we feel about, like, that version of dogfighting versus, like, shooting against the battleships?

00:20:59.780 --> 00:21:01.080
It was a lot more fun.

00:21:01.180 --> 00:21:02.580
Yeah. I thought it felt satisfying.

00:21:02.760 --> 00:21:05.980
Like, it felt, you know, you felt like you're hitting these ships.

00:21:06.160 --> 00:21:11.640
That, like, kind of basic, like, satisfaction of targeting something and then firing and nailing your shot.

00:21:11.980 --> 00:21:14.520
I did feel like I couldn't move as well as I wanted to.

00:21:14.940 --> 00:21:21.120
You know, like, not that my controls were stiff, but just that it wouldn't turn as much as I could.

00:21:21.480 --> 00:21:26.260
Yeah, definitely. I feel like a real plane might give you some force on that, too, though, right?

00:21:26.380 --> 00:21:29.480
Yeah. Like, I'm not saying, again, it's not a simulation, and I think that's to its credit.

00:21:29.700 --> 00:21:35.660
But I also thought, like, you know, it shouldn't just let me seamlessly, like, move completely over one way or the other.

00:21:35.780 --> 00:21:38.360
Like, the plane would give some fight higher up in the air.

00:21:38.960 --> 00:21:48.860
Yeah. I think that a lot of it is just because going off of, like, the illusion of control thing, no matter where you are, you're not going to be able to, like, avoid these guys.

00:21:49.060 --> 00:21:50.940
Right. They spawn on top of you, pretty much.

00:22:18.100 --> 00:22:20.900
Mm-hmm.

00:22:20.900 --> 00:22:22.960
It's different. I always went with the middle ones.

00:22:23.100 --> 00:22:24.300
Yeah, that's what I did. Did anybody try anything else?

00:22:24.300 --> 00:22:27.600
I just went with the top one the first time, just thinking, like, I have more.

00:22:27.840 --> 00:22:29.180
And then after that, I went with the middle ones.

00:22:29.260 --> 00:22:30.560
And I... That's what I did.

00:22:30.660 --> 00:22:34.340
Yeah. I guess I didn't really notice too much of a difference in the power.

00:22:34.700 --> 00:22:37.080
Like, maybe later in the game it gets more noticeable.

00:22:37.180 --> 00:22:47.260
Well, when you're trying to go to, like, air-to-ground or air-to-sea, like, the battleships and the tanks may take more than one of a certain variety and die in one hit from another.

00:22:47.560 --> 00:22:48.980
I thought, yeah, because I thought with the...

00:22:48.980 --> 00:22:52.640
Oh, you think it's, like, these missiles are better for battleships than these missiles?

00:22:52.640 --> 00:23:03.040
No, I think that whereas the middle one may take out a tank in one hit, it'll need two of the first kind, of the less powerful kind.

00:23:03.580 --> 00:23:07.040
Yeah, because I really only tried the first missiles on other aircraft.

00:23:07.260 --> 00:23:09.980
Yeah, me too. Yeah, and the missiles work great on the aircraft.

00:23:10.180 --> 00:23:14.080
Yeah. You know, most of them pretty much guarantee, like, that that aircraft is gone.

00:23:14.260 --> 00:23:16.320
Yeah, just like you. Yeah, and that makes sense, too.

00:23:16.600 --> 00:23:18.140
Aircraft gets hit by a missile, you're dead.

00:23:18.320 --> 00:23:20.600
You know? Like, I don't really know what to tell you.

00:23:21.260 --> 00:23:27.240
But also, like, I didn't mind that shooting was a valuable option, too.

00:23:27.340 --> 00:23:29.720
Like, you know, it felt almost like at first I was the missiles.

00:23:29.880 --> 00:23:30.840
I was like, oh, the missiles are great.

00:23:30.980 --> 00:23:33.040
Like, they lock on. They're going to pretty much guarantee a hit.

00:23:33.220 --> 00:23:36.200
But then I tried using the shooting, too, and it worked really well.

00:23:36.460 --> 00:23:38.960
The dogfighting in this is a lot better than Star Voyagers.

00:23:39.300 --> 00:23:45.460
Oh, yeah. Every one in 100 chance you run into a dogfighting situation, this was really good.

00:23:45.820 --> 00:23:49.940
Yeah, I think the aiming was a lot more maneuverable.

00:23:49.940 --> 00:23:59.040
I mean, whereas your plane itself may not feel very maneuverable, at least you can hit the guys you mean to hit.

00:24:00.380 --> 00:24:02.940
Like, going off of what Sam was saying.

00:24:03.100 --> 00:24:09.560
Yeah. And there's a lot of, like, they'll appear behind you and you have to figure out, like, what's my best strategy.

00:24:09.560 --> 00:24:17.160
I usually just try to, like, change altitudes and not, like, slow down.

00:24:17.600 --> 00:24:19.200
You can't slow down really.

00:24:19.300 --> 00:24:21.660
Well, I think it'd be during landing sequences.

00:24:21.780 --> 00:24:23.080
But only during refueling and landing.

00:24:23.300 --> 00:24:24.280
Yeah, refueling and landing.

00:24:24.520 --> 00:24:30.320
Yeah. So I think, like, mostly my strategy was just shake myself as much as possible to shake them off of me.

00:24:30.580 --> 00:24:31.420
And then...

00:24:31.420 --> 00:24:34.780
Are you talking about when there's a lock-on detected or when you see them down behind you?

00:24:34.780 --> 00:24:36.420
Even when I see them on my radar behind me.

00:24:36.520 --> 00:24:37.960
Which is really cool. We didn't talk about the radar.

00:24:38.100 --> 00:24:40.420
But I think that the radar is very appreciated as well.

00:24:40.560 --> 00:24:43.100
Yeah. Because it seems to sync up pretty well.

00:24:43.120 --> 00:24:45.860
And that's, like, a hard thing to program, I imagine.

00:24:46.100 --> 00:24:50.200
Yeah. A radar that also corresponds with where the enemies are in the game, too.

00:24:50.540 --> 00:24:56.040
Because it's, like, two separate spatial awarenesses, you know, for a game to register.

00:24:56.440 --> 00:24:57.440
So I appreciated that.

00:24:57.500 --> 00:24:58.440
I like all this stuff.

00:24:58.580 --> 00:25:00.080
Seems like we're pretty hot on the game, guys.

00:25:00.200 --> 00:25:01.220
Yeah. No one's complaining.

00:25:01.540 --> 00:25:02.400
No, I think it was fun.

00:25:02.400 --> 00:25:05.780
Let's talk about the landing. I think we should wait to get to the landing.

00:25:06.140 --> 00:25:07.680
Not only because...

00:25:07.680 --> 00:25:08.600
What's up? Sorry, no.

00:25:08.680 --> 00:25:10.080
I have something about the radar, but...

00:25:10.080 --> 00:25:11.840
Okay, yeah. Please say something about the radar.

00:25:12.140 --> 00:25:16.120
Just, I think that the radar's cool for seeing things that are coming up behind you and around

00:25:16.120 --> 00:25:17.340
you and stuff, but it's...

00:25:17.340 --> 00:25:18.860
I feel like it's too wide.

00:25:19.200 --> 00:25:24.240
Like, visually, it makes sense to be a square, but when you're just going forward and you

00:25:24.240 --> 00:25:29.100
really don't have the option to go left or right on your radar that much, like, your dot

00:25:29.100 --> 00:25:33.360
is strictly in the center and everything else is going to be in front or behind you.

00:25:33.620 --> 00:25:37.520
Yeah. So that just kind of becomes really apparent when you're looking at the radar that you

00:25:37.520 --> 00:25:38.660
really can't move that much.

00:25:38.760 --> 00:25:45.080
Yeah. One thing I did want to say in relation to the lock-ons.

00:25:45.080 --> 00:25:50.960
I think it's really cool that it has these things that will pop up that will make you

00:25:50.960 --> 00:25:53.340
have to sort of multitask.

00:25:55.740 --> 00:26:01.620
Because every once in a while in the game, you'll get a lock-on warning and it'll show

00:26:01.620 --> 00:26:10.680
you a graphic of your plane in relation to the first person of a missile about to hit you.

00:26:10.680 --> 00:26:16.040
And you sort of have to wiggle back and forth to get out of its way.

00:26:16.880 --> 00:26:20.220
And I think when you're doing that, while you're trying to hit other targets and also

00:26:20.220 --> 00:26:24.220
avoid incoming fire from the front of you, I think that that can get really tense.

00:26:24.340 --> 00:26:28.580
And I think that's to its credit instead of like a, oh god, I'm overwhelmed sort of feeling.

00:26:29.160 --> 00:26:33.240
Yeah. It does feel like, you know, you're kind of...

00:26:33.240 --> 00:26:34.360
On the edge of your seat.

00:26:34.380 --> 00:26:35.360
Yeah. You're on the edge of your seat.

00:26:35.480 --> 00:26:38.200
You're really battling, you know, the elements out there.

00:26:38.280 --> 00:26:39.440
Not the elements because it's...

00:26:39.440 --> 00:26:40.680
You're battling the weapons.

00:26:41.120 --> 00:26:42.140
You're battling the elements.

00:26:42.440 --> 00:26:43.780
That'll be funny. Children's clouds down.

00:26:44.200 --> 00:26:47.660
Weapons. No, but it feels like a dogfight.

00:26:47.820 --> 00:26:50.260
Yeah. The enemy planes don't just like take it either.

00:26:50.440 --> 00:26:55.080
You know, they do try to move out of your way when you're locking in on them or, you know,

00:26:55.080 --> 00:26:58.040
they kind of like... They don't zigzag, but they sway.

00:26:58.380 --> 00:26:59.440
They swoop. Yeah, they swoop.

00:27:00.060 --> 00:27:01.680
I like that. You do the swoops. You do the swoops and stuff.

00:27:01.780 --> 00:27:03.380
I think it's all awesome.

00:27:03.600 --> 00:27:05.540
Yeah. I'm a big fan of all this.

00:27:05.720 --> 00:27:11.260
And I also think like, what is communicated to you in the UI compared to that first Top

00:27:11.260 --> 00:27:12.860
Gun game that they said was more technical?

00:27:12.860 --> 00:27:16.060
I feel like this is pretty well established.

00:27:16.420 --> 00:27:18.080
Like you have... How many missiles are left?

00:27:18.140 --> 00:27:19.740
You have your altitude. You have your speed.

00:27:20.040 --> 00:27:22.180
You have that little radar thing.

00:27:22.280 --> 00:27:23.340
I don't know what else I'd include.

00:27:23.340 --> 00:27:26.940
I don't actually know what was included in the HUD for the original.

00:27:28.560 --> 00:27:29.480
It wasn't...

00:27:29.480 --> 00:27:31.260
There were no numbers essentially attached to it.

00:27:31.340 --> 00:27:33.700
It was a lot of meters going up and down.

00:27:33.880 --> 00:27:34.740
The game was more primitive.

00:27:34.940 --> 00:27:36.740
It was earlier in video games.

00:27:36.860 --> 00:27:41.180
But I'm just... I'm surprised that some people, you know, like...

00:27:41.180 --> 00:27:43.920
I wouldn't want to play that game at all after playing this one.

00:27:44.320 --> 00:27:45.560
This is such an improvement.

00:27:46.260 --> 00:27:53.240
And then it also has a couple other gameplay modes, I guess.

00:27:53.340 --> 00:28:00.680
Okay. The first of which that you'll probably work with is the refueling, which sort of just happens

00:28:00.680 --> 00:28:02.440
in the middle of any level.

00:28:02.600 --> 00:28:04.540
I think it's just time to happen.

00:28:04.760 --> 00:28:07.360
Well, you press start when it happens.

00:28:07.720 --> 00:28:08.540
But when you run out of fuel.

00:28:08.740 --> 00:28:11.180
Yeah, I think it's programmed to run out of fuel about halfway through.

00:28:11.480 --> 00:28:14.520
And you can call it in when you have missiles that are missing also.

