I think it's going to hold off on my essential games list vote for this because what would make this a great game that I would recommend to people still today is something like that.

01:10:01.220 --> 01:10:09.120
Seeing NES games in this style like this pseudo 3D thing they just don't translate well enough for me to like recommend playing today.

01:10:09.660 --> 01:10:14.440
But one thing Sean said that I think is really true is this is one of the best games on the console to date.

01:10:14.740 --> 01:10:17.360
I think that definitely like for me goes without saying.

01:10:17.560 --> 01:10:26.160
I think Konami is killing it and this is just another example of a way to offer something that nothing else on the console has offered yet.

01:10:26.300 --> 01:10:29.300
The only thing we could even say that it came close to was kind of like Star Voyager.

01:10:29.720 --> 01:10:30.860
But Star Voyager was garbage.

01:10:31.220 --> 01:10:33.700
You know like that was just a really like almost like a tech demo.

01:10:34.000 --> 01:10:36.320
Yeah. This is a full video game.

01:10:36.480 --> 01:10:45.040
And I think that if it was 1987 and you're big on Top Gun and you get this game, this game offers exactly what it's selling to you.

01:10:45.280 --> 01:10:48.940
I think the problem is that we're in 2019 and not 1987.

01:10:49.040 --> 01:10:52.800
And that's why I'm not putting it on the essential games list because it's not doing enough now.

01:10:52.980 --> 01:10:53.820
Yeah. Similar to.

01:10:53.920 --> 01:10:58.460
I totally agree. I would almost say like my feelings about this one, it's tough because I feel like it's like Metroid.

01:10:58.740 --> 01:11:01.580
You know, Metroid would have blown somebody's mind in 1987.

01:11:02.220 --> 01:11:12.240
Knowing what we have now, I don't think that Metroid is like still worth playing through because it's such a leap back from all the other great Metroid games.

01:11:12.240 --> 01:11:15.220
Let alone all the other great games that have been inspired by Metroid.

01:11:15.220 --> 01:11:27.400
I think that it'd be really tough for any first person style game to be on my essential games list for the NES because there's a lot of like I still have a lot of problems with modern first person games.

01:11:27.840 --> 01:11:29.960
I think it nailed the dog fighting.

01:11:30.160 --> 01:11:31.560
I think it got a little too difficult.

01:11:32.060 --> 01:11:34.620
The landing sequence thing, I'll admit, my bad.

01:11:34.740 --> 01:11:37.540
I think that's pretty cool that there is a way to do that.

01:11:37.620 --> 01:11:39.500
And I'm actually like, I'm down for that.

01:11:39.660 --> 01:11:44.820
I was mostly joking about the tension of the landing sequence.

01:11:44.820 --> 01:11:51.480
I just would have liked to have seen that same tensions applied to the game because I think like a missile being locked on.

01:11:51.600 --> 01:11:59.160
There is tension in the game. That missile being locked on to me did not feel nearly as stressful as landing and I just feel like what is more stressful than three missiles being targeted on to you?

01:11:59.220 --> 01:12:00.820
And I'll guarantee you, I'm dying on them.

01:12:01.060 --> 01:12:03.020
There's no way to get extra lives in the game.

01:12:03.200 --> 01:12:05.280
So the three lives you have is that's it.

01:12:05.700 --> 01:12:06.920
So good luck, you know?

01:12:08.120 --> 01:12:09.740
That said, I think it's a great game.

01:12:09.900 --> 01:12:13.400
I think we're all in the opinion that you should at least try it out and make your own opinion on it.

01:12:13.480 --> 01:12:15.560
Because I think some people are going to love it.

01:12:15.720 --> 01:12:16.960
Some people are going to hate it.

01:12:16.960 --> 01:12:25.700
And for those of us that played it, not me, but for those of you that played it 20 years ago, if you didn't know about that landing thing, maybe go back and check it.

01:12:25.720 --> 01:12:32.980
Because you might have some hidden skills in the dogfighting thing from playing it so many times that you might nail this landing thing and just progress right through the game.

01:12:33.200 --> 01:12:38.160
Like I said, I think this one definitely is one of the ones that teeters more on the edge than a lot of our games.

01:12:38.240 --> 01:12:41.660
A lot of times you can tell we're going to vote in the first impressions.

01:12:41.880 --> 01:12:43.540
We just give our essential games.

01:12:43.700 --> 01:12:53.040
Right, right. But yeah, and I also just wanted to say too that I think Sam said it really well as far as the way I feel is like something, just something missing.

01:12:53.640 --> 01:12:56.420
Like I wanted something just a little more to this game.

01:12:57.040 --> 01:12:58.280
But it is a close one.

01:12:59.200 --> 01:13:02.940
All right. And that is all the time we have for this episode of Nostalgia.

01:13:03.180 --> 01:13:04.980
I hope you'll join us again next Friday.

01:13:05.740 --> 01:13:11.940
In the meantime, if you want more Nostalgia, you can go to www.nostalgiacast.com.

01:13:12.080 --> 01:13:16.780
Got all sorts of fun things on our website, including every other episode we've recorded.

01:13:17.180 --> 01:13:19.140
And there's a little contact thing over there.

01:13:19.300 --> 01:13:23.760
You can contact us just like we had our guy earlier.

01:13:24.020 --> 01:13:24.960
Yeah, like mail. Yeah.

01:13:25.080 --> 01:13:25.940
It's like mail.

01:13:26.220 --> 01:13:27.560
Yeah, beefcake. Barber, beefcake.

01:13:27.560 --> 01:13:28.480
Oh yeah, beefcake barber.

01:13:28.640 --> 01:13:30.400
Beefcake barber. You decide.

01:13:30.600 --> 01:13:31.780
I don't want to dox the guy.

01:13:32.460 --> 01:13:37.200
You decide. All right, so does he cut the hair of beefcakes?

01:13:37.220 --> 01:13:39.080
Of beefcakes or is he a beefcake that cuts hair?

01:13:39.120 --> 01:13:40.440
Maybe his last name is Barber.

01:13:40.980 --> 01:13:42.480
Oh, I didn't think about that.

01:13:42.680 --> 01:13:44.120
Maybe his last name is Doctor.

01:13:46.780 --> 01:13:47.860
Barber Beefcake Doctor.

01:13:49.100 --> 01:13:51.580
Yeah, but he contacted us, so you should.

01:13:51.760 --> 01:13:53.300
Right? I'd love to hear your thoughts.

01:13:53.520 --> 01:13:56.060
You tell me if you were able to land that plane when you were eight.

01:13:56.060 --> 01:14:00.660
I bet you didn't, but I also bet you didn't just look below the jet like the rest of us did,

01:14:00.800 --> 01:14:02.340
because that's confusing.

01:14:02.660 --> 01:14:05.960
I feel like that's a Berenstain Bears thing, guys.

01:14:06.220 --> 01:14:07.200
Like, what is that about?

01:14:08.220 --> 01:14:09.180
It was there.

01:14:10.900 --> 01:14:15.100
And you know, while you're at it, we're on Twitter, at NostalgiaCast.

01:14:15.220 --> 01:14:17.060
We're on Gmail, NostalgiaCast.

01:14:17.920 --> 01:14:18.840
No one says that, right?

01:14:18.840 --> 01:14:20.560
I'm on Gmail. Yeah, we're on Gmail.

01:14:20.960 --> 01:14:23.540
Get me. Can't you slide into my Gmail?

01:14:23.540 --> 01:14:28.160
Yeah. We also, like, we're around, if you see us on the street.

01:14:28.400 --> 01:14:30.400
Yeah, if you hear our voices.

01:14:30.400 --> 01:14:33.820
Yeah, if you hear our voices talking on the street, they'll be afraid to come up to me and be like,

01:14:34.080 --> 01:14:36.220
hey, you're Joe from Nostalgia.

01:14:36.300 --> 01:14:37.540
And I'll be like, no, I just sound like Joe.

01:14:37.540 --> 01:14:38.640
I'm Mike from Nostalgia.

01:14:38.640 --> 01:14:41.500
If you think that Mike and I sound alike, please write in.

01:14:41.640 --> 01:14:44.680
If you think that Joe and I sound alike, please write in.

01:14:44.720 --> 01:14:47.540
I agree. Because we're told that a lot.

01:14:47.740 --> 01:14:50.200
And I get alarmed because I'm like, well, we do a podcast together.

01:14:50.200 --> 01:14:51.540
So hopefully people know who's talking.

01:14:51.640 --> 01:14:53.460
I don't think anybody who's sane thinks that.

01:14:53.460 --> 01:14:55.180
Right. That's true. People think.

01:14:55.620 --> 01:14:56.960
This is post-show material.

01:14:57.180 --> 01:14:59.880
